     widest SELF-LOCKING sliver w = 2.793 mm (half-angle = atan(mu=0.4) = 21.80 deg), seats 4.483 mm above the granule centre, crescent radius r_s = 4.707 mm
     90 deg conforming shard  arc   7.39 mm  A   20.65 mm2  F    7.43 N  ->  2.74x at recovery (20.4 N),  1.64x at normal current (12.2 N)
     180 deg conforming shard arc  14.79 mm  A   41.30 mm2  F   14.87 N  ->  1.37x at recovery (20.4 N),  0.82x at normal current (12.2 N)
     full-ring crescent       arc  29.57 mm  A   82.60 mm2  F   29.74 N  ->  0.69x at recovery (20.4 N),  0.41x at normal current (12.2 N)  <- STALLS
     (the round-5 granule-path critic derived the same bound independently on the r11 exports and got w = 2.791 mm -> 9.63 N (2.12x / 1.27x), 180 deg shard 19.26 N (1.06x / 0.63x), full ring 38.53 N (0.53x / 0.32x). Both constructions say the same thing: the backstop covers a partial shard and runs out at a full-ring crescent, where the drive STALLS rather than shears -- which is the intended failure mode, and it is now printed instead of implied.)

