EXIT KINEMATICS: the index is TWO-PHASE -- park(+22.5 deg) -> index 22.5 deg to the port -> DWELL -> index 22.5 deg to the next park. (a) release happens 3.25..10.50 deg INTO the first index, i.e. before the dwell begins, through a partial lune -- NOT from a stationary, concentric pocket (measured above); (b) the drop window is still a DWELL parameter, not a race -- fall time to clear the 14.5 mm pocket is 54 ms, so the contract dwell is 150 ms (2.8x); (c) the dwell is what guarantees the pellet is clear of the disc before the second index, and that part of the r6 argument survives.
exit drop line: straight vertical at (32, 0) -> 32 mm from the airframe centreline; chute bore Dia22 gives 4.5 mm of radial clearance around a worst-case pellet
IR beam at Z=-395.2 (40 mm below plate); v at beam = 0.89 m/s; occlusion ~17 ms (12 mm pellet + 3 mm beam); sensor faces recessed 5.0 mm from bore
chute ID 22.0 < 2xD: two-body arch needs two pellets in the chute; free-fall transit 101 ms << the two-phase cycle -> temporally excluded (rebuttal held from r2)
INTERFACE CONSTRAINT (r6, replaces r4's '>=150 ms index period'): the ICD command contract is INDEX 22.5 deg -> DWELL >= 150 ms -> INDEX 22.5 deg -> park; one pellet per 45 deg, <= 3 pellets/s. The dwell is the only timing the count loop depends on and it is a firmware constant, not a kinematic race.
