FILL-LINE RULE (r6): the MAX rib is the VOLUMETRIC brim line (421 pellets, 497 g). CONTEXT exempts pellet mass above the 250 baseline from the 1.5 kg ceiling, and the ceiling case is therefore the 250 load. For transparency the NO-EXEMPTION limits are printed too: on the quadruple-conservative ledger (CF-PETG 1.31 g/cm3, stepper 380 g gross, 100% infill, +10%) empty = 1323.4 g -> only 132 pellets, which is BELOW the 250 hard minimum: that reading is infeasible with a geared drive and r6 says so instead of quietly moving a rib. On the measured-infill ledger the same strict rule gives ~288 pellets. r5's rib was 393 on a 190 g direct drive.
SERVICE DRAIN: pellets below the funnel outlet + one pellet layer (z<-313.2) = 114 cm3 = ~50 pellets. That is the residue that can fall when the cartridge is dropped AFTER the documented drain (QR the payload, invert, remove the fill cap, pour back into the tub) -- not the 421-pellet load.

