SUMP APERTURE (measured at theta=190, z=-327.2): open radial runs ['8.00-15.00', '20.25-46.75']; the pellet window (the run containing the PCD) is r20.25..46.75 = 26.50 mm x 120.0 deg annular window; equivalent circular orifice D48.7. That is 2.04x the worst-case pellet -- CONCEPT-pocket-wheel 3's '~95 mm orifice' is WRONG and is struck in BUILD-NOTES-r5; the anti-bridging defence is the agitator, not the aperture size.

BEARING: iglidur-class flanged sleeve ID20.0/OD23.0, flange Dia30.0, journal length 7.0 mm at z -334.95..-327.95; seat probe (bushing vs housing counterbore) 0.00 mm3, hub-in-bore radial clearance 0.10 mm modeled. [D] p = 3 N / (20 x 7) = 0.0214 MPa vs iglidur J ~35 MPa static -> 1633x margin; L/D = 0.35 is short, so it constrains disc TILT and takes the bed load off the stepper bearings rather than acting as a precision journal (stated, not hidden).
  agitator self-capture: it is held by gravity alone, so inverting the payload for the service drain drops it off the hex. It cannot leave the hopper (OD 93 vs the Dia46 fill port) and the funnel outlet r47.5 limits its radial float to 0.8 mm, so on re-righting it lands concentric within 0.8 mm and drops onto the hex within 30 deg of hand rotation (45 deg lead-in chamfer modeled on the spigot top).
  agitator thrust face: rides on the bushing flange standing 0.30 mm proud of the sump floor (iglidur-on-TPU, not PETG-on-TPU); hex drive engagement 5.70 mm, 15.0 mm across flats, 0.4 mm AF clearance

