SERVICE PROCEDURE FACTS (measured, not narrated -- assembly NB-8):
  1. MOTOR IS NOT FIELD-REPLACEABLE IN PLACE. Driver columns on the 4 gearbox screws (r=13 bolt circle), +Z, 25 mm, vs every OTHER assembled solid: Dia1.5 -> 62.9104 mm3, Dia3.4 -> 322.3960 mm3, Dia6.0 -> 1475.8318 mm3, Dia8.0 -> 3463.0870 mm3 -> largest clear driver in situ = Dia0.0. The motor is fastened and removed ONLY as the plate+motor cartridge (that is what the quarter-turn latch is for).
  2. THE DISC MUST BE INDEXED TO theta = 202.5 deg before the grub can be fitted: the disc's grub pilot, the housing access port and the shaft flat only line up there (the continuous Dia2.6 void measured above is measured at that clocking). The grub must be pushed 43.00 mm radially down the Dia3.4 channel; there is no retrieval path if it is dropped in the chamber.
  2b. THE 4 x RX-M2x4 MOUNT INSERTS GO IN FROM THE UNDERSIDE of top_plate, while it is still a loose part (assembly r4 NB-1: 'a perfectly buildable sequence -- it is just not written anywhere'). Measured at (19, 19): Dia2.500 lead from the top face z=-181.550 down to -188.050, then the Dia3.200 x 4.000 mm insert bore, then a Dia4.800 relief shaft. A Dia3.2 insert cannot pass the Dia2.5 lead, so it is heat-set from below; the shoulder is a positive depth stop.
  4. LASH AT THE DRIVE-REACTION STOP is 0.5141 deg (assembly NB-4, measured on the r10 exports; free band -24.5142..+0.5142 deg, bounded to 2.4573 deg with the stop pin fitted). On a 22.5 deg index that is 2.28 % of a station of angular error the FIRST time the drive loads in each direction, and it must be in the count-contract text: the count is taken at the chute beam, not from the commanded angle, so lash cannot manufacture a count.
  5. SERVICE-STAND CLEARANCE is 8.000 mm (assembly NB-5): stand ground plane z=-426.45, lowest assembly solid = the motor can at z=-418.45. The load path is the meter_housing latch-ring underside on the stand's 3 pads -- printed structure, not the can.
  3. THE DISC MUST BE COUNTER-INDEXED BY THE UNLOCK ANGLE (-22 deg) when the cartridge goes in or out: the shaft D-flat and the disc D-bore flat are a keyed pair, so at the wrong relative angle the cartridge fouls the disc (the r3 critic measured 4.2552/4.6955/5.1242 mm3 at -20/-22/-24 deg and 0.0000 with the disc counter-indexed). The disc is free in the bearing until the grub is torqued, so this is a hand motion, not a fixture.

